Fig. 7.1 shows a circuit containing a capacitor of capacitance $C$ and a resistor of resistance $R$.

{{figure:figure_7_1}}

Fig. 7.1

Initially, the switch is open and the potential difference (p.d.) across the capacitor is $12\text{ V}$.

The switch is closed at time $t = 0$ and the capacitor discharges through the resistor.

Fig. 7.2 shows the variation of the charge $Q$ on the capacitor with the p.d. $V_{C}$ across the capacitor as the capacitor discharges. Fig. 7.3 shows the variation of the current $I$ in the resistor with the p.d. $V_{R}$ across the resistor as the capacitor discharges.

{{figure:figure_7_2}}

Fig. 7.2

{{figure:figure_7_3}}

Fig. 7.3

